--- body ---
## Context
The author proposed subtracting the language-specific component when centering
vectors for multilingual semantic retrieval. Track this as an empirical
hypothesis, not an adopted requirement or an established improvement.
Ticket 0031 covers library-wide calibration; this question concerns the geometry
of cross-language retrieval and is independent of its fraction-RRF trigger.

## Exploration
Compare unchanged embeddings, global mean centering, and a language-conditioned
correction. Specify whether the correction subtracts the full language centroid
or only its offset from the global centroid; apply the chosen transform to both
queries and documents and document normalization order. Estimate corrections
using training data only, with topic-matched or parallel-language controls to
separate language effects from differences in subject matter. Include mixed and
unknown language inputs and sparse-language estimates.

Use the Multilingual Menagerie and the cross-lingual probe (closed ticket 0266)
as starting points. Evaluate cross-language retrieval, same-language retrieval,
hubness, and per-language regressions on held-out material. Any adoption rule or
new design threshold needs the normal DECISIONS.md ruling and SPEC.md ownership.
No runtime implementation or upstream filing is authorized by this research note.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Reproducible comparison with disjoint estimation and evaluation material
- [ ] Report benefits, regressions, and topic/language confounding
- [ ] Recommend adopt, reject, or further measurement with evidence
